       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Even for a 70 kg patient with normal liver function, that dose risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure. Many institutions also cap the daily dose at 3,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, split another way\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
